{
    "_notes": "Infineon (Cypress) CY8CMBR3106S CapSense Express touch controller at 0x37, its default (the address is part of its stored configuration), as on MikroE's Cap Touch 5 click. 8-bit registers; the configuration (0x00-0x7E, with a CRC at 0x7E) is held in the chip's flash and applied with a command, so this record doesn't write it: which sensors are buttons and which make up a slider is the board's stored setting. In deep sleep (within 0.6 s of the last transfer, on the bench) it NACKs the transfer that wakes it, then answers: \"wakeNack\" has the bus try a NACKed access to it once more, without which the scanner, probing each address seconds apart, never finds it\nDetection: FAMILY_ID (0x8F) = 0x9A and DEVICE_ID (0x90-0x91, little-endian) = 0x0A06\nInit: none\nPoll (100 ms): 10 bytes from BUTTON_STAT (0xAA): BUTTON_STAT (0xAA-0xAB, one bit per sensor CS0-CS5, 1 touched), LATCHED_BUTTON_STAT (0xAC-0xAD), 0xAE-0xAF, SLIDER1_POSITION (0xB0), LIFTOFF_SLIDER1_POSITION (0xB1), SLIDER2_POSITION (0xB2), LIFTOFF_SLIDER2_POSITION (0xB3). A slider position is 0xFF when it isn't touched (or there is no slider). MikroE's library names CS3, CS0, CS2 and CS1 the click's buttons 1-4\nSource: registers from the Infineon CY8CMBR3xxx register TRM",
    "addresses": "0x37",
    "wakeNack": true,
    "detectionValues": "0x8f=0x9a&0x90=0x060a",
